  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-08-06T20:23:38.478Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The personal mirror belongs to the PlayerLocal layer in build 1220. I think that the PlayerLocal layer is not appropriate for the mirror because it is not a part of avatars and should be separable from avatars.\nAlso, some photographers discovered the value of this mirror for broadening their expression. For example:\n- https://twitter.com/_maido39_/status/1554492318505660416\n- https://twitter.com/Bismuth833/status/1553311817665245184\nTherefore, I want an option to make the mirror can be visible from the VR camera.\nCould you consider using different layers for the personal mirror?\n----\nThe followings are some candidates and my opinion:\nPickupNoEnvironment/UI switchable:\nI recommend this option first to maximize expressiveness, but it increases the complexity of the feature.\nUI layer:\nIt is the second best solution in my opinion because it is very simple and controlling the visibility of UIs is already implemented for the VR camera.\nHowever, hiding other UI objects (e.g., HUD, nameplates, UIs in worlds) is required for photo-shooting with the mirror. It is troublesome and sometimes may be impossible.\nConsideration of UI/UiMenu vs. Reserved2:\nRecently VRChat added the Reserved2 layer for some UIs, but it is not suitable for the mirror because mirrors should be affected by post-processing. Therefore, the UI layer is a good choice if you select from UI-like layers.\nI think that my proposal is better than the current implementation but may not be the best. Please comment if someone has other good proposals.\nRelated issues:\n- https://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/1216please-add-toggle-to-turn-off-personal-mirror-in-vrcamera",
